# Unreal
Binaries/
Build/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Plugins/
*.VC.db
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.sln
*.suo
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/

# Headless core build
build/
Tools/HeadlessBuild/build/
match.json
*.rep

# The compliance scanner and its policy live under build/Compliance and MUST be
# tracked: CI runs them, and ADR-011 makes them a release gate. The negations are
# spelled with the lowercase path because that is what git actually holds -- the
# earlier capital-B version could never match on a case-insensitive filesystem, so
# the scanner was silently untracked and CI failed on every push for its whole
# history without anyone seeing why.
!build/Compliance/
!build/Compliance/**
build/Compliance/**/__pycache__/

# Python leftovers from an unrelated project in this directory
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# OS
.DS_Store

# Generated SoundWave assets: reproduced from the WAVs in Audio/ and
# Content/RA4/Audio/ by "UnrealEditor RedAlert4.uproject -run=RA4AudioImport".
# ~590 binary assets that would otherwise be committed twice, once as source
# audio and once as engine assets.
/Content/RA4/Audio/Generated/
/Content/RA4/Generated/

# Ignore binary asset files (.uasset, .umap) by default: generated and imported
# content should not bloat history.
*.uasset
*.umap

# UI art and widgets are hand-authored and the interface breaks without them, so
# they are versioned. Without this exception every newly imported texture was
# silently dropped from its commit and only surfaced as a missing background on
# a fresh clone.
!/Content/RA4UI/Art/**/*.uasset
!/Content/RA4UI/Widgets/**/*.uasset
!/Content/RA4UI/Fonts/**/*.uasset


# Kimi work-state reports must persist between iterations
!Saved/Reports/
!Saved/Reports/**

# Headless CMake build artifacts. The wildcard matters: the existing rule only
# caught "build/", so a "build-audit/" tree slipped past it and 705 .o/.o.d/.make
# files were committed -- with paths still naming Documents/red-alert-4, the
# directory this project had before it was renamed.
/Tools/HeadlessBuild/build/
/Tools/HeadlessBuild/build-*/

# FactoryEnvironment: a 7 GB third-party environment pack that was never tracked
# in git, is referenced by no map, no material and no source file, and was the
# sole source of 208 of the 212 errors from a full-package ResavePackages -verify
# run (152 LogBlueprint + 95 LogScript). Those errors made every full-package
# commandlet exit non-zero, which hides real regressions. Moved out of Content/
# rather than deleted; see Docs/Production/THIRD_PARTY_PACK_AUDIT.md.
/Content/ThirdParty/FactoryEnvironment/

# Editor/merge scratch files. A stray SimWorld.cpp.t -- a 136 KB copy of the
# simulation core, six months stale, in no build -- was committed by a failed
# revert and sat in the tree unnoticed. A second copy of the core is exactly the
# duplicate-subsystem hazard the project rules forbid, and it is worse when it
# looks like source.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*.cpp.t
*.h.t
*~
